      "start_seconds": 0.58,
      "end_seconds": 3.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Good morning. I've just opened your notes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 4.66,
      "end_seconds": 5.78,
      "duration_seconds": 1.12,
      "text": "Hi, thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.35,
      "end_seconds": 9.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "start wherever you like, I'm listening"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.69,
      "end_seconds": 15.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "Um, so... swollen face. That's why I came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.12,
      "end_seconds": 20.19,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "so, which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.86,
      "end_seconds": 31.09,
      "duration_seconds": 7.23,
      "text": "I'm on clopidogrel, 75 milligrams, once a day. Allopurinol, 300 milligrams, started four weeks ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.29,
      "end_seconds": 51.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Did it come on recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.46,
      "end_seconds": 55.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "I've had it since Monday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.58,
      "end_seconds": 60.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "Is it constant or in episodes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.82,
      "end_seconds": 64.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "I'd say on and off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.0,
      "end_seconds": 69.63,
      "duration_seconds": 4.63,
      "text": "Right, any breathing difficulty, mouth sores or blisters at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 70.24,
      "end_seconds": 74.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "Right, no, I haven't had any of them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.06,
      "end_seconds": 78.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 80.11,
      "end_seconds": 83.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "That's normal as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.49,
      "end_seconds": 88.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "Has your heart given you any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.16,
      "end_seconds": 90.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.49,
      "text": "Nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.63,
      "end_seconds": 106.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "so, how active are you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 108.11,
      "end_seconds": 112.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "I hardly move around during the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.92,
      "end_seconds": 116.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "Tell me about your eating."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.56,
      "end_seconds": 122.61,
      "duration_seconds": 5.05,
      "text": "I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.97,
      "end_seconds": 141.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.99,
      "end_seconds": 144.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "No, not at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.02,
      "end_seconds": 151.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "Has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.15,
      "end_seconds": 157.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.34,
      "text": "Yes, plasters. I get a red itchy rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.31,
      "end_seconds": 160.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "what about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.89,
      "end_seconds": 169.94,
      "duration_seconds": 8.05,
      "text": "I've had heart disease for two years now. I've never really been one for hospitals."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.51,
      "end_seconds": 174.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "Has anyone in your family had anything serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.49,
      "end_seconds": 177.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "My father has Parkinson's disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 196.54,
      "end_seconds": 208.41,
      "duration_seconds": 11.87,
      "text": "doctor, I've got the the readings for you oxygen saturation is 98 percent, respiratory rate 18. Pressure 109 over 72, pulse is 101 beats a minute, temperature is 38.6 degrees"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.28,
      "end_seconds": 211.2,
      "duration_seconds": 0.92,
      "text": "okay, noted"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.26,
      "end_seconds": 214.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "let's move on to the examination"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 216.82,
      "end_seconds": 217.76,
      "duration_seconds": 0.94,
      "text": "that's alright"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.8,
      "end_seconds": 220.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "hold that for a second"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.6,
      "end_seconds": 243.2,
      "duration_seconds": 7.6,
      "text": "There is a widespread red rash, facial swelling, and your temperature is high with enlarged glands."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.86,
      "end_seconds": 259.42,
      "duration_seconds": 11.56,
      "text": "Okay, you can relax now. Okay, thinking it through, I'm honestly not certain yet. It could be a severe drug reaction, or it might be a viral rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 260.08,
      "end_seconds": 263.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "Mm, do you think it's something serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.7,
      "end_seconds": 305.18,
      "duration_seconds": 35.48,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like a severe drug reaction, but I'd like to confirm. I'll request urgent blood tests, it'll help with severe drug reaction. I'll start you on prednisolone, 40 milligrams, once a day, until review. That's for severe drug reaction. Stop the allopurinol now and you need admission. If the symptoms get worse, or you feel really unwell, please come to the emergency department."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 305.9,
      "end_seconds": 308.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "okay, um, makes sense"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.45,
      "end_seconds": 315.45,
      "duration_seconds": 6.0,
      "text": "Come back straight away. Is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 315.95,
      "end_seconds": 317.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "that's clear, thanks"
    }
  ]
}